# hooks/docker-makefile.ts carried a raw NUL byte as a token sentinel, which made
# git classify it as binary — an 8KB change to the command guardrail rendered as
# "Bin 14353 -> 22776 bytes" and was invisible to `git diff`, to GitHub's PR view,
# and to any diff-based review. The byte is now written as the `\0` escape, but
# git compares against the old blob too, so without this the next diff of that
# file is still binary. Forcing a text diff makes the guardrail reviewable.
*.ts diff
*.js diff
*.json diff
